REQUEST_VERSION 1.0.0

ID REQUEST-0017

STATUS APPROVED

DATE 2026-07-27

WHO External adopter (independent project) relayed by President Cley Duarte

SCOPE PACE

TITLE

Second real-world feedback after testing PACE 0.3.0 against a live
project: two findings, both accepted and fixed in 0.3.1.

RAW_TEXT

(1) Cosmetic: after supersede, the old file keeps STATUS ACTIVE
internally; only ACTIVE_VERSIONS knows it is no longer current. Cleaner
if supersede also stamped the old file SUPERSEDED. (2) Real bug: pace
update runs pip install --upgrade without --break-system-packages, so it
fails on modern Debian/Ubuntu externally-managed (PEP 668) environments.
Everything else worked exactly as described; the most important gap
(handoff ignoring CONTINUITY.md) is genuinely resolved.

PROPOSED_SCOPE PACE

DESIGN_NOTE

Both fixed for 0.3.1: (1) supersede now stamps the prior version file
STATUS SUPERSEDED + SUPERSEDED_BY <new>, a lifecycle metadata update (the
same sanctioned exception the contract already grants requests STATUS) -
files are now self-describing, not dependent on ACTIVE_VERSIONS alone.
(2) pace update now retries with --break-system-packages when the plain
upgrade fails, and the final hint includes the flag. The report confirms
0.3.0 resolved the primary reported gap - this is validation, not just
bug-finding.

PROMOTED_TO

F6-34 (pace update PEP 668 fallback) + F6-35 (supersede stamps prior file)

APPROVED_BY

President Cley Duarte

END
